ef 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1031 "Factoring Linear Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1033 87 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051079 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7f29909c-8f45-5a17-820a-13a0a327cd5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186203491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186203492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186203493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186203494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186203495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186203491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203490 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b9422b9e-c65d-596a-90ac-20fde363b97c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203491 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203491 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203491 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8639ce62-5e23-5361-b682-c7000582d54e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203492 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203492 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203492 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f6b1d5cd-7280-5a3b-b538-d976044c6e94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203493 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203493 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203493 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fcfa0123-90e9-5186-b54d-3ae7859972b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203494 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203494 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203494 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3cb6287c-2e23-513c-b813-c514eaaaaae3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203495 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203495 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203495 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7dffe079-6e58-5eee-a2d4-f50f9c6c606c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203852 #edb/ref 1069 "e-17087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203852 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$\n\nII. $2z - 5 = z + 1$\n\nIII. $3z - 2 = 3z - 2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203852 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd07ad0f-548a-5569-84de-d658a88c4b9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203852 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z+3 & =4z+9 \\\\ 4z+3-4z & =4z+9-4z \\\\ 3 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z-5 & =z+1 \\\\ 2z-5-z+5 & =z+1-z+5 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2z - 5 = z + 1$ has the unique solution $z = 6.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z-2 & =3z-2 \\\\ 3z-2-3z & =3z-2-3z \\\\ -2 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203853 #edb/ref 1069 "e-17213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203853 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n4(r - 2)y = -8\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203853 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cba9196c-fdc3-594d-a1ad-948cf75bd366" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203853 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay = b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na = 4(r - 2), \\qquad b = -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4(r - 2) = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(r-2) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4(r-2)}{4} & =\\frac{0}{4} \\\\ r-2 & =0 \\\\ r & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203854 #edb/ref 1069 "e-17214" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203854 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2nx + 7  = -4x + 5\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $n?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203854 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "36eadc0b-c2b0-5f84-8f39-2b8399932edb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203854 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ax = b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $4x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2nx+7 & =-4x+5 \\\\ 2nx+4x+7 & =-4x+5+4x \\\\ 2nx+4x+7 & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2nx+4x+7 & =5 \\\\ 2nx+4x+7-7 & =5-7 \\\\ 2nx+4x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(2n + 4)x  = -2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(2n + 4)}_{a}x  = \\underbrace{-2}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2n + 4= 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+4 & =0 \\\\ 2n+4-4 & =0-4 \\\\ 2n & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{2n}{2} & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\ n & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203878 #edb/ref 1069 "e-18853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203878 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n(r - 9)z + 2 = -1\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203878 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5ee14499-89b0-59a3-9f13-b0a00c0e518d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186203878 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax = b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\neq 0.$ If $a = 0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-9)z+2 & =-1 \\\\ (r-9)z+2-2 & =-1-2 \\\\ {{(r-9)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{-3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nr - 9 = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-9 & =0 \\\\ r & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186476177 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186203852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204089 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving For an Unknown Parameter" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186203853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204090 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477030 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477031 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477034 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477035 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477039 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186477042 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186203878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204091 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186204599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477046 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477050 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477060 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477062 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186477066 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186477074 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186203854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204092 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186205041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1045 "Linear Equations With No Solutions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186205035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1050 600.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186204177 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "de17f2e1-7eda-5a05-b05f-fc9631097dd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204596 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186203490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204596 #edb/ref 1069 "q-287665" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204596 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204596 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2px=3\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204596 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6c453dd-3b6b-5f65-bf37-1fc261d1f26a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204596 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=b.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=2p,\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2p=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\np=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204597 #edb/ref 1069 "q-287667" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204597 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204597 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(p-4)x+2=5\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38670cb7-04d7-5bd3-bbc0-32b596369870" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186204597 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4)x+2 & =5 \\\\ 2(p-4)x+2-2 & =5-2 \\\\ {{2(p-4)}_{⏟}}_{a}x & ={{3}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(p-4)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(p-4) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(p-4)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ p-4 & =0 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1061 476517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b8a4ffe-a6bc-5748-9925-775d621ef0ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205035 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1061 476518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2a517a1e-2402-5834-92c6-d387d20f3740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205036 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1061 476521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a4d784bb-4dc8-51b7-9c57-1caf81eeaf95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205037 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1061 476522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "15db0382-7d51-5840-b3da-75384a89354d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205038 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186205207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1061 476523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8211e280-4fa1-564c-9189-09c44ee53dde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205039 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186205041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1061 476526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16595ce8-f055-561b-9a7f-397923fee1b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205040 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1061 476529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eddfa8ae-b5d6-5ef0-ba45-f6c57207ae16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205041 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186204092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1064 "Some linear equations can have **no solutions.** This means there is no value of $x$ that can be substituted into the equation to give a true statement.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following equation:\n\n$$\nx+1 = x\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to solve this equation. We start by subtracting $x$ from both sides.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x \\\\ x+1\\,-\\,x & =x\\,-\\,x \\\\ (x-x)+1 & =(x-x) \\\\ 0+1 & =0 \\\\ 1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the final equation, $1=0,$ is always **false**. In other words, there is no value of $x$ that we can substitute to make the equation true. \n\nTherefore, our equation has no solutions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1065 11390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ae552721-c050-5d83-9cfc-347accbc894b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205174 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n7qx = -5,\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solutions, what is the value of $q?$\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax = b{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7q}_{\\large a} \\ x = \\underbrace{-5}_{\\large b}\n$$\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\na = 7q, \\qquad b = -5.\n$$\n\nWe know that an equation of the form $ax=b$ with $b \\neq 0$ has no solutions when $a = 0.$\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n7q = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7q & =0 \\\\ \\frac{7q}{7} & =\\frac{0}{7} \\\\ q & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the equation $7qx = -5$ has no solutions if $q = 0.$\n\n**Note:** The constant $q$ in this problem is sometimes called a **parameter.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1065 13402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d31382b3-ae61-5a9e-a3bf-53f71f939a5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205207 #edb/ref 1067 "Problems Involving Unknown Parameters" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, suppose we have an equation in the variable $x$ of the form \n\n$$\nax = b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n- $b$ is *not* equal to zero, which we write as $b \\neq 0.$\n\nThen, if $a = 0,$ the equation has **no solutions.**\n\nIndeed, by substituting $a = 0$ into $ax=b,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ax & =b \\\\ (0)x & =b \\\\ 0 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a *contradiction* (i.e., a statement that's always false) because we were told that $b \\neq 0.$ Therefore, the equation has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1065 13428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8a5cc3be-1b56-5e46-8944-f75697b65b59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186205208 #edb/ref 1067 "Conditions for an Equation To Have No Solutions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295510 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295510 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295510 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ae663b6-85c5-5077-b87c-a6180d34333b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295592 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295592 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295592 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38f1f5d0-a65b-50e5-ae53-71603b6a4f59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295695 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{4}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295695 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295695 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b4fa932-686f-5272-80f1-319a4616fc55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295759 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295759 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295759 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5513a93f-ae93-5de6-bdce-765af89d5be4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296297 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296297 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296297 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c2937687-dedd-5964-bb4d-22153fc13d86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296346 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296346 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296346 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cdfab9aa-d797-5176-8659-fc606759afe0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296591 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296591 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296591 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f950fb0f-6b6e-53ca-bbe7-61f27fce1157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296644 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296644 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296644 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296644 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186295592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296644 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0392835c-e04b-5ad0-8c8d-d5dc8f5281c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186295759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186296346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296681 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1839f0af-c2f8-56ec-a3e2-a0f1a0ec6286" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296775 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186296297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296775 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296775 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296775 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186296297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186296775 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4a06a891-d4f2-506a-bdd0-0692d7f6be31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439052 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439053 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186439054 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288066" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-3u+4=-3u-1$\n- **II.** $2u+5=2u+8$\n- **III.** $6u-2=3u+1$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b892079-10a1-5d68-a34f-01695fac566e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297172 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3u+4 & =-3u-1 \\\\ -3u+4+3u & =-3u-1+3u \\\\ 4 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $-3u+4=-3u-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+5 & =2u+8 \\\\ 2u+5-2u & =2u+8-2u \\\\ 5 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $2u+5=2u+8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6u-2 & =3u+1 \\\\ 6u-2-3u+2 & =3u+1-3u+2 \\\\ 3u & =3 \\\\ u & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $6u-2=3u+1$ has the unique solution $u=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297205 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297205 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288662" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297205 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297205 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $y,$ given by\n\n$$\n3py=5y+8\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297205 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cf4ece6-fb8b-5a6f-963d-f97832f4331b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297205 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ay=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $5y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3py & =5y+8 \\\\ 3py-5y & =5y+8-5y \\\\ 3py-5y & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $y$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(3p-5)y=8.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ay=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(3p-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}y={{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n3p-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-5 & =0 \\\\ 3p-5+5 & =0+5 \\\\ 3p & =5 \\\\ \\frac{3p}{3} & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297209 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297209 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288678" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297209 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297209 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-3pz-8=-z-6\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297209 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93ece185-5396-5f04-8ab8-086b4b609861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297209 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $az=b.$ \n\nWe start by adding $z$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz-8 & =-z-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-z-6+z \\\\ -3pz+z-8 & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3pz+z-8 & =-6 \\\\ -3pz+z-8+8 & =-6+8 \\\\ -3pz+z & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $z$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(-3p+1)z=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(-3p+1)}_{⏟}}_{a}z={{2}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-3p+1=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3p+1 & =0 \\\\ -3p+1-1 & =0-1 \\\\ -3p & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{-3p}{-3} & =\\frac{-1}{-3} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186438046 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438046 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438046 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "533b9094-d677-5376-88f4-8f426a2a4cf6" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438047 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438047 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438047 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b5a3d38-5a54-5a47-a0a8-64956fa7cdee" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438048 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438048 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438048 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38767ef4-49fe-519a-b838-3b77b5b7521b" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438049 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438049 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438049 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36138474-e8c9-5d26-acfa-e3b7ef2f057d" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438050 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438050 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438050 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4435d623-199a-5d01-8347-ab72dc2191c8" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438051 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438051 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186438051 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83476a1a-ee79-50fd-b7a1-580c8914eb50" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439052 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186438046 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439052 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186438047 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439052 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439052 #edb/ref 1077 "I" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439052 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186438047 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439052 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bd3eb9cd-0eda-53a6-bbc3-9f6bfbd15e06" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439053 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186438048 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439053 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186438049 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439053 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439053 #edb/ref 1077 "II" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439053 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186438049 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439053 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e6d2fdbb-10bc-55e5-8c2c-6df645004975" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186439054 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186438050 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [175921