=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "353a2e9f-97dd-52cc-88ff-dcca6d9658cb" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477031 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $aw=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(r-5)w-6 & =4 \\\\ 5(r-5)w-6+6 & =4+6 \\\\ {{5(r-5)}_{⏟}}_{a}w & ={{10}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5(r-5)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(r-5) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5(r-5)}{5} & =\\frac{0}{5} \\\\ r-5 & =0 \\\\ r & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477038 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(q+5)v+6=-4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "498d8977-f2e3-576d-98c6-e159e4faf155" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477034 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q+5)v+6 & =-4 \\\\ 2(q+5)v+6-6 & =-4-6 \\\\ {{2(q+5)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{-10}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(q+5)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q+5) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(q+5)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ q+5 & =0 \\\\ q & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477037 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477035 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #ed