17592186477066 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $au=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $9u$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4qu+4 & =9u-8 \\\\ 4qu-9u+4 & =9u-8-9u \\\\ 4qu-9u+4 & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $4$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4qu-9u+4 & =-8 \\\\ 4qu-9u+4-4 & =-8-4 \\\\ 4qu-9u & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $u$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(4q-9)u=-12.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(4q-9)}_{⏟}}_{a}u={{-12}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4q-9=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4q-9 & =0 \\\\ 4q-9+9 & =0+9 \\\\ 4q & =9 \\\\ \\frac{4q}{4} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ q & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477074 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186204092.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477074 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "b2b16748-3249-59b8-8679-78daaba7b541" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186507616 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507616 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507616 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c78cb3d-2cc5-5e2c-9e55-a80e139339bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507644 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507644 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507644 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "27628a6f-5c23-5872-87a7-878f2e1da6b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507663 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507663 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507663 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "306bd0fa-00bf-5a91-966b-275a7a3521a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507684 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507684 #edb/ref 