47 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508031 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508031 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508031 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508031 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fa2138e2-b337-52b3-8a3d-5fd1ad2f1eba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508045 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508045 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288639" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508045 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508045 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $v,$ given by\n\n$$\n2(q-7)v+5=1\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508045 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f18d6f2-f26d-5ef1-84dd-3ecfcc80ad41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508045 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $av=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q-7)v+5 & =1 \\\\ 2(q-7)v+5-5 & =1-5 \\\\ {{2(q-7)}_{⏟}}_{a}v & ={{-4}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2(q-7)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(q-7) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(q-7)}{2} & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\ q-7 & =0 \\\\ q & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508071 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508071 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508071 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508071 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $t,$ given by\n\n$$\n5qt=-4\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508071 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6feec1bb-9d5b-5e0f-99d7-930f0577f85b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508071 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $at=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=5q,\\,b=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n5q=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\nq=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508100 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508100 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288069" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508100 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508100 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $2x-3=2x+4$\n\nII. $-5x+7=-2x-2$\n\nIII. $4x+1=4x+1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508100 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0bffce7-58da-5042-ae7f-fb5de551e1a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508100 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =2x+4 \\\\ 2x-3-2x & =2x+4-2x \\\\ -3 & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2x-3=2x+4$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+7 & =-2x-2 \\\\ -5x+7+2x-7 & =-2x-2+2x-7 \\\\ -3x & =-9 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-5x+7=-2x-2$ has the unique solution $x=3.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+1 & =4x+1 \\\\ 4x+1-4x & =4x+1-4x \\\\ 1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508108 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508108 #edb/ref 1069 "q-288637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508108 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508108 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the equation in the variable $z,$ given by\n\n$$\n-7(k+3)z+8=1\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508108 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e39fec5d-501d-5ef0-88cc-5eeb84d919b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508108 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(k+3)z+8 & =1 \\\\ -7(k+3)z+8-8 & =1-8 \\\\ {{-7(k+3)}_{⏟}}_{a}z & ={{-7}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-7(k+3)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(k+3) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{-7(k+3)}{-7} & =\\frac{0}{-7} \\\\ k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
